@robertsmark6365 When the song was released, YouTube was still 15 years away from even existing. Even so, it must have well over 100 million views spread across many videos, and billions throughout history from being played on radio and television. Besides, view counts are not a meaningful measure of anything in the world of football. Keep in mind that countries such as India, China, Indonesia, Pakistan, the United States, Bangladesh, etc., generate huge numbers of views from people who may have little or no knowledge of the sport. In the football world, that is, among genuine fans, there is no debate: “Un’estate italiana” is always chosen as the best and most beloved one. 
"Dai Dai" 2026 song, 350 million, is a really low number for a World Cup anthem in the 21st century, when almost the entire planet has access to the internet. It is clearly a failure from every point of view. 
Add the following factor to the equation. Much of today’s music is very basic, musically poor, and heavily reliant on autotune. It may have millions of followers and streams, but no one with real musical knowledge would say it is better.

